Proposed change to the desktop's edge scroller, ~/.config/hypr/scripts/scroll-edge.py (outside this repo; not applied
by anything here). Optional: XR Workspace works with it applied or not (docs/technical.md, "With scroll-edge.py").

Its edge loop leaves the left / right edges of the XR-n desktops to XR Workspace, which scrolls their columns itself
before a push there switches desktops (tools/native_spike/columns.py). Click-to-reveal still acts on every output.
Fixes: one owner for those edges, so no second scroll for one step even on a loaded machine; and scroll-edge.py no
longer scrolls the neighbouring XR desktop when the hand briefly pushes the cursor onto its edge.

Made against the file as of 2026-11-03 (sha256 3b2be9241ba7685307eb64672c9d31e13595a41544aed8a914db753185cbbbc5).
Apply, then restart it:
    cd ~/.config/hypr/scripts && patch -p1 < /path/to/viture-workspace/docs/scroll-edge-skip-xr.patch
    ./scroll-edge.py --stop; sleep 1; ./scroll-edge.py --toggle

